# 🎓 DTU Chat Assistant — A RAG Chatbot for the Technical University of Denmark

[![Streamlit App](https://static.streamlit.io/badges/streamlit_badge_black_white.svg)](https://dtu-chatbot.streamlit.app/)

This repository contains the implementation of a Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) chatbot developed as part of the *Advanced Business Analytics* course at the Technical University of Denmark (DTU).

It is designed to support DTU Master's students by making it easier to access and understand key academic information — from course prerequisites to program requirements and exam dates.

## 🤖 About This Chatbot

Navigating a Master’s program can be overwhelming. This assistant makes it easy to access key academic info—like course prerequisites, program requirements—via natural language queries.

Whether you're starting your MSc or planning your electives, the assistant can help with:

- Mandatory and elective course structures  
- Course details: ECTS, prerequisites, instructors, semesters  
- Graduation and exam requirements  
- Cross-program course eligibility  
- Study plan support and recommendations  

💡 Select your MSc program from the sidebar to get tailored answers.  
Try asking:
- *“What are the mandatory courses for MSc Computer Science?”*  
- *“Can I take 01005 Linear Algebra as an elective?”*  
- *“How many ECTS do I need to graduate?”*

---

## 📌 Objective

We aim to make DTU's academic information more accessible and user-friendly by combining deep learning with information retrieval. The chatbot answers practical questions that students typically struggle with by leveraging official DTU data.

---

## 🔍 Dataset

The knowledge base is created via web scraping from:
- [kurser.dtu.dk](https://kurser.dtu.dk/search) – for course details  
- [sdb.dtu.dk](https://sdb.dtu.dk) – for program structures and exam info

---

## 🧠 Tech Stack

- **Embeddings**:
  - `text-embedding-3-small` (OpenAI) — used for general text and document chunks  
  - `paraphrase-MiniLM-L6-v2` (SentenceTransformers) — used for short texts like course names
- **Vector Store**: Weaviate
- **Language Model**: OpenAI GPT
- **Frontend**: Streamlit
- **Data Collection**: Web scraping via BeautifulSoup, requests
- **Data Processing**: custom chunking strategies
